  "slug": "cafe",
  "title": "Cafe Color Palettes",
  "tagline": "Roasted, steeped, and served — color combinations for coffee culture.",
  "description": "The best cafes have a visual warmth that makes you want to stay. It is not accidental. The palette of coffee culture runs from the deep brown of espresso to the ivory of steamed milk, from the terracotta of Japanese hand-thrown cups to the warm gold of afternoon light through a window. Wada's catalog captures all of this in combinations that predate the third-wave coffee aesthetic by decades. These palettes work for cafe branding, packaging for roasters and specialty food producers, restaurant interior concepts, and any project that should feel like a warm room on a cold morning.",
